{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change","id":940210,"title":"Fate 2 is still broken post-errata (no Informed needed) and Steadfast needs to change","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T13:19:12-07:00","id":940210,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Fate 2 is still broken post-errata (no Informed needed) and Steadfast needs to change","content":"The new Mage 2e errata leaves spells like Space 1's The Outward and Inward Eye ambiguous in a critically important fashion, Time 2's Veil of Moments system-breaking by RAW, and Time 4's Prophecy completely Social maneuvering-destroying, but let us focus on something even more egregious that was completely untouched by errata: Fate boons being able to grant Steadfast.<br /> <br /> How did this receive no errata at all? Let us see what is still possible with a middling Fate-user with Gnosis 2, Fate 2, an Order Rote Skill at 4 dots, and a Rote for Exceptional Luck. Since the Informed Condition is sketchy on its RAW validity, we will be eschewing its usage here.<br /> <br /> For context, according to DaveB, if you are casting magic under time constraints and/or pressure and fail, you take a cumulative -1 penalty on subsequent attempts. If you are under neither time constraints nor pressure, you must use the &quot;down and dirty spellcasting&quot; rules, which prevents you from using Yantra bonuses or spell factors:<br /> <a href=\"https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47571978\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47571978</a><br /> <a href=\"https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47572307\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47572307</a><br /> <a href=\"https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47572307\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47572307</a><br /> <a href=\"https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47578204\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47565839/#47578204</a><br /> <br /> Additionally, Fate 2's Exceptional Luck costs Mana in order for it to grant a bonus beyond +5:<br /> <a href=\"https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47578117/#47579868\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47578117/#47579868</a><br /> <br /> Neither was included in the errata, but neither was denied by the errata either, so let us assume DaveB's rulings above still apply.<br /> <br /> None of the following were changed by the errata either:<br /> \u2022 Page 111 of Mage 2e says, &quot;The penalties to spellcasting can exceed the normal \u20135 penalty cap to dice pools. In cases where the penalty would reduce the dice pool beyond 0 \u2014 and thereby a chance die \u2014 by an additional \u20135 even after including bonuses from Yantras, the spell is too complex for the mage to cast and it automatically fails.&quot; This should not be an issue if the final pool is -5.<br /> \u2022 The rule concerning spell stacking in page 118 concerns &quot;multiple spells [affecting] the same aspect of the character,&quot; which does not prevent a single spell from buffing the dice pool for the same spell about to be recast.<br /> \u2022 Page 119 tells us that &quot;a mage can draw upon one Yantra as a reflexive action when casting a spell.&quot;<br /> \u2022 According to page 134, a single hex/boon can have its Potency split up to cover multiple effects. However, this is still a single hex, just like the example with &quot;a Potency 4 hex allows the mage to levy a penalty on the subject's next two actions, as well as apply the Blinded and Leg Wrack Tilts&quot; shows us. Likewise, &quot;boons that affect the same skill do not combine their effects (only the highest bonus counts),&quot; but this should not be a problem if we are relying on only one boon and are not actually trying to stack numerical bonuses together.<br /> \u2022 Page 136 lets +2 Reach allow the entire boon from Fate 2's Exceptional Luck to affect spellcasting rolls, and another +2 Reach and 1 Mana can allow the spell to be cast as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> Let us examine four scenarios.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> <u><b>Scenario A:</b></u> The mage is in a calm situation and would like to succeed at a mundane task\u2014any mundane task at all, even something absurdly difficult such as succeeding on an unskilled roll with an additional -5 penalty for difficulty.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #1:</b> Cast Exceptional Luck. One Reach for instant action casting, one Reach for Advanced Duration, one Reach for Advanced Potency. One leftover Reach. Mudra Yantra, but no bonus from it.<br /> Dice pool: Gnosis 2 + Fate 2 = 4 dice, for an ~75.22% chance of regular success and a ~0.77% chance of exceptional success. If this roll fails, since this is a calm scene, the spell can simply be reattempted.<br /> Result: Potency 2 Exceptional Luck lasting for an hour. Allocated to 9-again or chance-die-to-regular-die on the next dice roll and the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #2:</b> The mage now attempts the task with a 100% chance of earning at least one success. No matter how many penalties are levied against them, the boon will always convert a chance die to a regular die, and if that fails, Steadfast can trigger for an automatic success.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> <u><b>Scenario B:</b></u> The mage is in a tense scenario and would like to cast an extremely powerful spell, not necessarily a Fate spell. They are completely out of time; they need to cast the spell this very instant, during their turn, perhaps because they are embroiled in combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #1:</b> Cast Exceptional Luck. Two Reaches and 1 Mana for reflexive action casting, two Reaches to affect spellcasting. Mudra Yantra.<br /> Dice pool: Gnosis 2 + Fate 2 + Mudra 5 = 9 dice, for a ~78.69% chance of regular success and a ~17.27% chance of exceptional success.<br /> Result: Potency 2 Exceptional Luck lasting for a turn, affecting spellcasting. Allocated to 9-again or chance-die-to-regular-die on the next dice roll and the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #2:</b> Cast a spell as an instant action. The mage can take enough spell factor penalties to push themselves down to -5 and then automatically succeed thanks to their boon.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost of the above:</b> 1 Mana, assuming no exceptional success occurs.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> <b><u>Scenario C:</u></b> The mage is in a tense scenario and would like to cast an extremely powerful spell, not necessarily a Fate spell. However, they have two turns (six seconds) of prep time, possibly because they are not actually in combat.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #1:</b> Cast Exceptional Luck. One Reach for instant action casting, one Reach for Advanced Duration, two Reaches to affect spellcasting. Mudra Yantra.<br /> Dice pool: Gnosis 2 + Fate 2 + Mudra 5 = 9 dice, for a ~78.69% chance of regular success and a ~17.27% chance of exceptional success.<br /> Result: Potency 2 Exceptional Luck lasting for an hour, affecting spellcasting. Allocated to 9-again or chance-die-to-regular-die on the next dice roll and the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #2:</b> Cast Exceptional Luck. One Reach for instant action casting, one Reach for Advanced Duration, two Reaches to affect spellcasting. Mudra Yantra. -10 spell factor to improve to Potency 7, -4 spell factor for three turn duration.<br /> Dice pool: Gnosis 2 + Fate 2 + Mudra 5 - spell factors 14 = -5 dice, turned into an automatic success by the previous boon.<br /> Result: Potency 7 Exceptional Luck lasting for three turns, affecting spellcasting. Allocated to 9-again or chance-die-to-regular-die on the next dice roll, the Steadfast Condition, and a +5 bonus to the mage's next five spellcasting rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #3:</b> Dismiss the first instance of Exceptional Luck.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #4:</b> Cast a spell as an instant action. The mage can take enough spell factor penalties to push themselves down to -5 and then automatically succeed thanks to their boon, and the +5 bonus to spellcasting gives them even greater leeway.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost of the above:</b> Two turns.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> <b><u>Scenario D:</u></b> The mage is in a tense scenario and would like to inflict premeditated murder upon someone. They have no prep time at all; they are embroiled in combat and need to inflict murder right here, right now.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #1:</b> Cast Exceptional Luck. Two Reaches and 1 Mana for reflexive action casting, one Reach for Advanced Duration, one Reach for Advanced Potency. Mudra Yantra.<br /> Dice pool: Gnosis 2 + Fate 2 + Mudra 5 = 9 dice, for a ~78.69% chance of regular success and a ~17.27% chance of exceptional success.<br /> Result: Potency 2 Exceptional Luck lasting for an hour. Allocated to 9-again or chance-die-to-regular-die on the next dice roll and the Steadfast Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #2:</b> Cast Exceptional Luck. Two Reaches and 1 Mana for reflexive action casting, one Reach for Advanced Duration, one Reach for Advanced Potency. Mudra Yantra. -4 spell factor to improve to Potency 4.<br /> Dice pool: Gnosis 2 + Fate 2 + Mudra 5 - spell factor 4 = 5 dice, for an ~81.17% chance of regular success and a ~2.02% chance of exceptional success<br /> Result: Potency 4 Exceptional Luck lasting for an hour. Allocated to +4 bonus to next four [Athletics, Brawl, Firearms, or Weaponry] rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #3:</b> The mage commits premeditated murder and provokes an Act of Hubris.<br /> <br /> <b>Step #4:</b> Even if the Storyteller levies penalties that reduce the mage's dice pool for degeneration down to -5, the first Exceptional Luck's boon transforms the roll into an automatic success, preventing Wisdom loss. As a cherry on top, &quot;Any time your character risks Wisdom degeneration, she gains an Arcane Beat. Exploring the depths of hubris can be enlightening.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Cost of the above:</b> 2 Mana, assuming no exceptional successes occur.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> I do think that the above is enough to warrant the replacement of Steadfast in Fate boons with something more reasonable. After all, the above requires only Gnosis 2 and Fate 2, nothing more.<br /> <br /> Steadfast should not just change for Fate boons, but for all spells as well, since the creative thaumaturgy subsystem arguably allows for a two-dot Ruling spell to create Steadfast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11912,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","user":"Earth Seraph Edna","date":". 07-30-2016, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T17:11:17-07:00","id":940349,"title":"","content":"I feel like the forum's had this discussion before.<br /> <br /> The solution is simple:<br /> <br /> You aren't allowed to stack effects from boons like you do with hexes. You can't get the 9-again/chance-die-to-single-die and Steadfast to the same roll.<br /> <br /> Scenario D doesn't work because Wisdom checks are not mundane rolls, and are not spell-casting rolls. You can't apply boons to them without a spell that specifies it can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:19:10-07:00","id":940445,"title":"","content":"No You already had one thread<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls\"> Steadfast and automatically succeeding on degeneration rolls - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Page 126 of Mage 2e tells us: &amp;quot;Ruling (&bull;&bull;) spells can create most non-Persistent, mundane Conditions.&amp;quot; Likewise, one of the options in page 115 for an exceptional success on spellcasting is: &amp;quot;A Condition which will give Arcane Beats when resolved, on either the mage or her subject.&amp;quot; STEADFAST Your character is confident and resolved. When you&rsquo;ve failed a roll, you may choose to resolve this Condition to instead treat the action as if you&rsquo;d rolled a single success. If the roll is a chance die, you may choose to resolve this Condition and roll a single regular die instead. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:08:32-07:00","id":940470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940349#post940349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the forum's had this discussion before.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a post-errata version of the above with less need for dubious interpretations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The solution is simple:<br /> <br /> You aren't allowed to stack effects from boons like you do with hexes. You can't get the 9-again/chance-die-to-single-die and Steadfast to the same roll. </div> </div> </div>That would still allow Steadfast on its own, for pushing spell dice pools down to 1 and then automatically succeeding anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scenario D doesn't work because Wisdom checks are not mundane rolls, and are not spell-casting rolls. You can't apply boons to them without a spell that specifies it can. </div> </div> </div>Nothing about Steadfast specifies that it functions only with mundane rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:29:11-07:00","id":940481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Earth Seraph Edna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940470#post940470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a post-errata version of the above with less need for dubious interpretations.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you note though, nothing changed, so nothing in this discussion ends up changing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would still allow Steadfast on its own, for pushing spell dice pools down to 1 and then automatically succeeding anyway. </div> </div> </div>Yep. Which isn't really that big of a boost all things considered. It's also only succeeding it one success, which limits the overall utility of this. And since Boons can't generated Conditions you already have, you have to recast every time you want to use Steadfast, which is time and/or mana consuming to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing about Steadfast specifies that it functions only with mundane rolls. </div> </div> </div>Boons granted by Fate only apply to mundane rolls be default. That's why you need to use Reach to apply Boon bonuses to spell-casting.<br /> <br /> If you get Steadfast from something else and want to save it to use on a Wisdom check, that's different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T23:09:46-07:00","id":940498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940481#post940481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Which isn't really that big of a boost all things considered. It's also only succeeding it one success, which limits the overall utility of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>One success is all that is necessary for a spell heavily upgraded by spell factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940481#post940481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And since Boons can't generated Conditions you already have, you have to recast every time you want to use Steadfast, which is time and/or mana consuming to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>In tense situations, the Mana cost is low and can be mitigated by exceptional successes. In calm situations, there is no need to spend Mana at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940481#post940481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boons granted by Fate only apply to mundane rolls be default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this stated? As far as I can tell, the only Fate boon that affects only mundane rolls is the first bullet point under boons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T01:04:41-07:00","id":940530,"title":"","content":"If a player of mine tried this exploit (edit: Scenario D) I'd just rule that they get the success until the spell expires, at which point they have to roll the Degeneration. Degeneration is your soul getting twisted by things you've done wrong, you can postpone dealing with it via magic, but that's not something Fate 2 can hold off indefinitely. Or, if they try, they'll have to deal with cumulative Degeneration rolls, a permanently occupied spell slot and an inability to get any more Fate boons.<br /> <br /> Edit: Scenario A is you being a supernatural creature. That is design as intended.<br /> Scenario B&amp;C won't happen because you're using magic to gain magic. That ain't Fate 2. You may as well say the Perfecting Practice of Mind should let you get Rotes or Arcana. Otherwise we can have Fate mages casting so they can use stronger Fate magic so they can use stronger Fate magic so they can use... Ad infinitum.<br /> <br /> Also, you can't double up on 9-again with it. You'd be suppressing one Boon with another, the more powerful taking effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","user":"AinSoph","date":". 07-31-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T02:21:26-07:00","id":940544,"title":"","content":"The opening post mentions that this part has been untouched by the terrata, so how is this any different than that pre-errata thread? Fine, might as well say the thing in a newer thread.<br /> <br /> For Wisdom, simple solution is that generally nothing affects Wisdom degeneration rolls.<br /> <br /> As for the Steadfast thing, fine, you get a cca +5, beating the Potency calc by 4, congrats, creative.<br /> You need 1 die for Steadfast to apply (no, you can't first change chance to 1 then succeed on 1) , meaning you effectively get a bonus of 4 to 5, certainly more safely as even a bigger pool has a fail chance, but it's not a fail chance you can reasonably count on - you still need proper Yantras and whatevers to get a powerful spell, even at 1 die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:31:46-07:00","id":940566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Earth Seraph Edna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940498#post940498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One success is all that is necessary for a spell heavily upgraded by spell factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's no better than, say, getting +5 dice from the dice boon. It's slightly more reliable, but the +5 dice could roll an exceptional success. If you're cool with Exceptional Luck being able to give dice bonuses to rolls, Steadfast at 1 die isn't really all that different in the long run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In tense situations, the Mana cost is low and can be mitigated by exceptional successes. In calm situations, there is no need to spend Mana at all. </div> </div> </div>Rolling an exceptional success on the Exceptional Luck roll is not going to be common enough to mitigate the Mana cost.<br /> <br /> As well you can't get an exceptional success out of Steadfast unless you reduce yourself to a chance die and hope to roll five (or 3 for a Praxis) straight 10s in a row, so you're not getting exceptional successes out of the Steadfast boosted magic either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is this stated? As far as I can tell, the only Fate boon that affects only mundane rolls is the first bullet point under boons. </div> </div> </div>If that were the case/how you want to read the passage, than you could give yourself Steadfast without extra Reach to affect spell-casting rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:35:52-07:00","id":940600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940530#post940530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Scenario A is you being a supernatural creature. That is design as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not so sure about this. This is a low-cost investment (two dots in an Arcanum) that assures at least one success on any mundane task no matter how difficult it might be and no matter how inept and unskilled the mage is, for virtually no cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940530#post940530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scenario B&amp;C won't happen because you're using magic to gain magic. That ain't Fate 2. You may as well say the Perfecting Practice of Mind should let you get Rotes or Arcana. Otherwise we can have Fate mages casting so they can use stronger Fate magic so they can use stronger Fate magic so they can use... Ad infinitum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is exactly what the rules allow, since +2 Reach is being spent to affect spellcasting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AinSoph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940530#post940530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you can't double up on 9-again with it. You'd be suppressing one Boon with another, the more powerful taking effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are activating 9-again or turn-chance-die-into-regular-die from the Fate boon, and then Steadfast. Neither conflict with one another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940566#post940566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's no better than, say, getting +5 dice from the dice boon. It's slightly more reliable, but the +5 dice could roll an exceptional success. If you're cool with Exceptional Luck being able to give dice bonuses to rolls, Steadfast at 1 die isn't really all that different in the long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>The +5 bonus is more difficult to work for because that takes 5 Potency. In a tense situation wherein you have a couple of turns of preparation time, you ideally want the 9-again or chance-die-into-regular die benefit, Steadfast, <b>and</b> a +5 bonus, as scenario B shows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940566#post940566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rolling an exceptional success on the Exceptional Luck roll is not going to be common enough to mitigate the Mana cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Mana and a reflexive action to hypercharge a spell far better than Prime can seems like a good deal to me. We are speaking of Fate 2 here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940566#post940566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well you can't get an exceptional success out of Steadfast unless you reduce yourself to a chance die and hope to roll five (or 3 for a Praxis) straight 10s in a row, so you're not getting exceptional successes out of the Steadfast boosted magic either.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the spells themselves are far more powerful due to vastly boosted spell factors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940566#post940566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that were the case/how you want to read the passage, than you could give yourself Steadfast without extra Reach to affect spell-casting rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAI, probably not. RAW, absolutely, as there is no limitation against this. What you want the &quot;this affects spellcasting&quot; Reach option for is the 9-again or chance-die-into-regular-die benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:32:43-07:00","id":940750,"title":"","content":"Ok, a few things rather than point by point:<br /> <br /> 1) Yes, performing one mundane task you have more than a chance die in at 1 automatic success per casting of a spell is things working as intended. Lots of supernatural powers provide equivalent bonuses (or far better) at low level. Also see point 2.<br /> <br /> 2) One success is all an action needs to succeed, but that doesn't mean you succeed well enough. If the action is Contested? Then your opponent is probably going to beat your one success. Is the action scaled? Well then your one success jump probably isn't going to be enough to get you to that next building. Is the action Extended? 1 automatic success per roll probably means you fail unless the required number of successes is less than your base dice pool. For magic specifically, is the spell Withstood? Because all the spell factors in the world aren't going to do squat if you get stopped because your base Potency isn't high enough to get around the needed amount in case of Withstood.<br /> <br /> 3) Shifting goal posts doesn't help conversations. The counter to, &quot;exceptional successes aren't common enough to negate the overall mana costs racking up,&quot; is not, &quot;well it's worth the mana.&quot;<br /> <br /> 4) In this particular case, we're both talking about RAI, because the RAW are not actually as clear as people that tend to argue Fate 2 as broken make it out to be. In other threads about this, I've made very full arguments about how my take on the RAW is different from the take of the RAW you are using (and nobody came up with a single reason why the way I present the text to be read was incorrect from just the text alone). You have to accept that you're stating a specific interpretation of the rules (one that seems to stem from trying to read the rules as technically as possible, despite the authors extolling us not to).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T13:04:11-07:00","id":940777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940750#post940750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Yes, performing one mundane task you have more than a chance die in at 1 automatic success per casting of a spell is things working as intended. Lots of supernatural powers provide equivalent bonuses (or far better) at low level. Also see point 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is also free and works with anything no matter how many penalties are levied against you. If you have, say, Intelligence 2, no ranks in a mental skill (-3 penalty), and are attempting an absurdly difficult feat under that skill (-5 penalty), you would normally have a dice pool of -6. A single resource-free casting of Fate 2's Exceptional Luck covers you there, earning you a single success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940750#post940750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) One success is all an action needs to succeed, but that doesn't mean you succeed well enough. If the action is Contested? Then your opponent is probably going to beat your one success. Is the action scaled? Well then your one success jump probably isn't going to be enough to get you to that next building. Is the action Extended? 1 automatic success per roll probably means you fail unless the required number of successes is less than your base dice pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct here. You underestimate just how many actions are the type that only need one success, however. As per pages 70-72 of the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook, arguments, carousing, fast-talk, interrogation, intimidation, investigating a scene, repair, and research all take only one success. Likewise, investigation only ever needs a single success to find a clue, and social maneuvering takes a contested roll only some of the time.<br /> <br /> Going by pages 79-80 of the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook, a character with, say, Intelligence 2 and Investigation 0 (-3 unskilled) wanting to investigate a crime scene over a year old (-5 penalty) that they have a personal grudge towards (-2), that has had its evidence impeccably tampered with (-5) and that aligns with their Vice (-2) while alone (-1) and extremely pressed for time (-3) would have a -19 dice pool. With a no-casting cost of Exceptional Luck, they earn a single success anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940750#post940750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For magic specifically, is the spell Withstood? Because all the spell factors in the world aren't going to do squat if you get stopped because your base Potency isn't high enough to get around the needed amount in case of Withstood.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is absolutely wrong. Spell factors can be used to increase Potency, and 9-again or chance-die-into-regular-die plus Steadfast is an incredibly effective method of raising spell factors and thus potency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940750#post940750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Shifting goal posts doesn't help conversations. The counter to, &quot;exceptional successes aren't common enough to negate the overall mana costs racking up,&quot; is not, &quot;well it's worth the mana.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not moving goalposts when I had already laid clear the Mana costs in my opening post. Considering how easy it is for a mage to regain Mana in a calm scene simply by spamming a spell they have a Praxis for, Mana is hardly an issue. Remember that as per DaveB, failing on spellcasting rolls outside of tense situations does not incur the cumulative -1 penalty; they do use the &quot;down and dirty&quot; spellcasting rules, but that does not prevent Praxis usage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) In this particular case, we're both talking about RAI, because the RAW are not actually as clear as people that tend to argue Fate 2 as broken make it out to be. In other threads about this, I've made very full arguments about how my take on the RAW is different from the take of the RAW you are using (and nobody came up with a single reason why the way I present the text to be read was incorrect from just the text alone). You have to accept that you're stating a specific interpretation of the rules (one that seems to stem from trying to read the rules as technically as possible, despite the authors extolling us not to). </div> </div> </div>Errata is a perfect avenue through which developers can clarify and rebalance rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T16:34:17-07:00","id":940918,"title":"","content":"It's growing painfully clear that you're the type of person that approaches the &quot;RAW&quot; as, &quot;Rules as Read as Stupidly as Possible,&quot; rather than what the rules actually say. I understand the urge to try to identify flaws in the game as an exercise to discover things people might want to change for their own games. But these conversations never go anywhere because there's no way to convince someone else that the RAW are not the most broken way you can possibly read the rules when that's how they choose to approach the rules.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't actually need an errata. Sure, it would be nice if Dave clarified it, but in half a dozen threads on these, even the people that decry how &quot;broken&quot; the rules will concede every way to read the rules in a not-stupid fashion as being valid. But that never matters, because reading the rules smart means you had to use your brain, which means it can't be &quot;RAW.&quot; Tough. Your thread has no point because nobody really cares about patting you on the head for pointing out how stupid the rules can be when you read them specifically to maximize stupid results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T18:19:31-07:00","id":940976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940918#post940918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's growing painfully clear that you're the type of person that approaches the &quot;RAW&quot; as, &quot;Rules as Read as Stupidly as Possible,&quot; rather than what the rules actually say. I understand the urge to try to identify flaws in the game as an exercise to discover things people might want to change for their own games. But these conversations never go anywhere because there's no way to convince someone else that the RAW are not the most broken way you can possibly read the rules when that's how they choose to approach the rules.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't actually need an errata. Sure, it would be nice if Dave clarified it, but in half a dozen threads on these, even the people that decry how &quot;broken&quot; the rules will concede every way to read the rules in a not-stupid fashion as being valid. But that never matters, because reading the rules smart means you had to use your brain, which means it can't be &quot;RAW.&quot; Tough. Your thread has no point because nobody really cares about patting you on the head for pointing out how stupid the rules can be when you read them specifically to maximize stupid results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not entirely sure what you were expecting from a book that allows a certain ability to grant X and have it be compatible with Y, then avail of X under Y.<br /> <br /> X is Steadfast, and Y is spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Is there an unspoken RAI that they were never intended to intersect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11912-earth-seraph-edna","name":"Earth Seraph Edna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T20:32:57-07:00","id":941014,"title":"","content":"The book isn't the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T22:30:19-07:00","id":941041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940918#post940918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's growing painfully clear that you're the type of person that approaches the &quot;RAW&quot; as, &quot;Rules as Read as Stupidly as Possible,&quot; rather than what the rules actually say. I understand the urge to try to identify flaws in the game as an exercise to discover things people might want to change for their own games. But these conversations never go anywhere because there's no way to convince someone else that the RAW are not the most broken way you can possibly read the rules when that's how they choose to approach the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>The RAW is whatever the book says. Call us stupid all you want, it doesn't change the facts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have to accept that you're stating a specific interpretation of the rules (one that seems to stem from trying to read the rules as technically as possible, despite the authors extolling us not to). </div> </div> </div>That is not a reasonable stance. Technical readings exist for clarity. If a technical reading gives a different result than what was intended, then the text is not clear enough, and needs errata.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book doesn't actually need an errata. Sure, it would be nice if Dave clarified it, but in half a dozen threads on these, even the people that decry how &quot;broken&quot; the rules will concede every way to read the rules in a not-stupid fashion as being valid. But that never matters, because reading the rules smart means you had to use your brain, which means it can't be &quot;RAW.&quot; Tough. Your thread has no point because nobody really cares about patting you on the head for pointing out how stupid the rules can be when you read them specifically to maximize stupid results. </div> </div> </div>We're not interpreting a religious text. We're reading a rulebook. Rulebooks in RPGs exist so that everyone is on the same page. Unambiguity is critical to that. If you don't care about ambiguity, then why not toss out the rulebook and rely on Storyteller fiat? If you're going to make ambiguous rules that require you to read between the lines and interpret the implications of these ten pages, but not those ten pages, then you might as well throw those rule sections out entirely and write your own, because they're not accomplishing anything useful, and they're actively creating distractions and wasting time. If the rulebook can't state all of its assumptions, and relies on you to pick and choose some implications, but not others, then it's a flawed rulebook that could benefit from errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","user":"Strill","date":". 08-01-2016, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T22:42:16-07:00","id":941044,"title":"","content":"Guys, I will repeat what I said last time: why do we care responding to this guys? In fact I suspect Edna is just a sock puppet for Strill. <br /> <br /> It is clear this guys dont really want to play a game and have fun, they just want to pick a fight. <br /> <br /> And even if they aren't, they are just taking this thing waaaaaay too seriously. Its just a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T22:47:30-07:00","id":941046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=941044#post941044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is clear this guys dont really want to play a game and have fun, they just want to pick a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's picking fights? As far as I'm concerned, understanding the rules is a game in and of itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Guys, I will repeat what I said last time: why do we care responding to this guys? In fact I suspect Edna is just a sock puppet for Strill. </div> </div> </div>Hahaha, I imagine Edna will get a kick out of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And even if they aren't, they are just taking this thing waaaaaay too seriously. Its just a game. </div> </div> </div>Seriously how? Putting a lot of thought into something doesn't mean you're taking it too seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T23:27:33-07:00","id":941064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940445#post940445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No You already had one thread<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls\"> Steadfast and automatically succeeding on degeneration rolls - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/909108-steadfast-and-automatically-succeeding-on-degeneration-rolls </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Page 126 of Mage 2e tells us: &amp;quot;Ruling (&bull;&bull;) spells can create most non-Persistent, mundane Conditions.&amp;quot; Likewise, one of the options in page 115 for an exceptional success on spellcasting is: &amp;quot;A Condition which will give Arcane Beats when resolved, on either the mage or her subject.&amp;quot; STEADFAST Your character is confident and resolved. When you&rsquo;ve failed a roll, you may choose to resolve this Condition to instead treat the action as if you&rsquo;d rolled a single success. If the roll is a chance die, you may choose to resolve this Condition and roll a single regular die instead. </div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tried to warn yah","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T23:58:55-07:00","id":941076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=940750#post940750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) In this particular case, we're both talking about RAI, because the RAW are not actually as clear as people that tend to argue Fate 2 as broken make it out to be. In other threads about this, I've made very full arguments about how my take on the RAW is different from the take of the RAW you are using (and nobody came up with a single reason why the way I present the text to be read was incorrect from just the text alone). You have to accept that you're stating a specific interpretation of the rules (one that seems to stem from trying to read the rules as technically as possible, despite the authors extolling us not to).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna frame and print this. Put it on a ruler and slap people in the face with it....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T02:22:05-07:00","id":941108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=941041#post941041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The RAW is whatever the book says. Call us stupid all you want, it doesn't change the facts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not calling you stupid. I'm saying that when you and the OP drone on about what the books, &quot;technically,&quot; mean, you actually are going on about, &quot;the results of purposefully reading the text in as stupid a way as possible.&quot; If you have fun doing that, that's cool. The issue is when you insist that having fun examining what happens when you read the text to achieve the maximum amount of silly results whenever the need to interpret the text arises, is the same as actually finding broken rules that need to be addressed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is not a reasonable stance. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is. If you're told the text is not written in strenuous technical language, but opts to use natural language, it is unreasonable to treat the text as if it were written in strenuous technical language as the sole basis for something being &quot;broken.&quot;<br /> <br /> As has been demonstrated repeatedly, lots of people manage to figure out the intention of the text without it being up to your personal standards on clarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're not interpreting a religious text. We're reading a rulebook. </div> </div> </div>It's funny how similar these two activities are though. The difference is theology is done for its own sake. RPG books serve a purpose, and the writing only needs to be precise enough to facilitate that purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you don't care about ambiguity, then why not toss out the rulebook and rely on Storyteller fiat? </div> </div> </div>If you want books that never have ambiguity in them, why aren't you burning your money instead of buying any of the majority of RPGs out there?<br /> <br /> Though, your fallaciously constructed false equivalence only furthers the idea that your concept of &quot;technical&quot; reading is skewed to the point of being useless. The issue is that in your (and the OP's) &quot;technical&quot; reading, you throw out <i>critical</i> reading, which is the far more important skill.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T03:02:49-07:00","id":941117,"title":"","content":"In addition, as somebody who is actually making his living with writing and reading stuff you might call &quot;technical texts&quot;, I can assure you, that even those are not always as crystal clear as Strill and Edna think they might be. Even those need proper context and indexing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T03:34:54-07:00","id":941125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=941044#post941044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact I suspect Edna is just a sock puppet for Strill.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny, I had just begun to suspect that very thing and then you posted this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T08:07:57-07:00","id":941197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/940210-fate-2-is-still-broken-post-errata-no-informed-needed-and-steadfast-needs-to-change?p=941044#post941044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guys, I will repeat what I said last time: why do we care responding to this guys? In fact I suspect Edna is just a sock puppet for Strill. <br /> <br /> It is clear this guys dont really want to play a game and have fun, they just want to pick a fight. <br /> <br /> And even if they aren't, they are just taking this thing waaaaaay too seriously. Its just a game.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Guys, if you suspect something like this, just flag one of their posts and explain it in the report. Publicly ccusing people of being sockpuppets and/or trolls like this is pushing personal attack territory, and not flagging them makes it take longer for the mods to find out about it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T16:51:35-07:00","id":941510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted b